% Test cases for the ostomy supplies policy (ostomy_supplies.le): synthetic
% claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33828 and per payment condition
% of dmepos.le and Policy Article A52487. Findings are recorded as the
% treating practitioner's, the reviewer's or the Council's; a finding
% nobody made leaves the answer conditional. Supplies are a one-off or a
% refill: no rental month. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the
% first query, so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and
% necessary, and what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base ostomy_supplies cases includes these resources:
    ostomy_supplies.

the knowledge base ostomy_supplies cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a month of drainable pouches with filter (A4416, 60
% a month) for a permanent colostomy: the practitioner's judgment of
% permanence, the colostomy status code on the claim, and every
% documentation requirement in the record. The prosthetic benefit asks
% nothing about the residence; no code of the policy is on the CMS
% face-to-face list.
scenario pouches_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the pouches.
    the HCPCS code of the pouches is "A4416".
    the pouches is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 60.
    the ostomy of Ann is colostomy.
    the finding permanent impairment requiring ostomy about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "end colostomy after abdominoperineal resection for rectal cancer; no reversal is planned".
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "Z93.3".
    the order for the pouches is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the pouches is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the pouches includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the pouches includes order date.
    the order for the pouches includes description of the item.
    the order for the pouches includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the pouches includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the pouches was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the pouches was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the pouches.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The usual maximum quantities: 40 skin barriers with flange (A4414, 20 a
% month) for two months are within it, 50 are not; 16 adhesive remover
% units (A4455, 16 per 6 months) for three months are within it, 20 are
% not; a pouch with convex barrier (A4413), not in the table, has no usual
% maximum. The reviewer finds no explanation for more in Ben's record.
scenario usual_quantities is:
    claim 1 is for the barriers.
    the HCPCS code of the barriers is "A4414".
    the barriers is furnished to Ben.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 2 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 40.
    claim 2 is for the extra barriers.
    the HCPCS code of the extra barriers is "A4414".
    the extra barriers is furnished to Ben.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 2 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 50.
    claim 3 is for the adhesive remover.
    the HCPCS code of the adhesive remover is "A4455".
    the adhesive remover is furnished to Ben.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 3 is 16.
    claim 4 is for the extra adhesive remover.
    the HCPCS code of the extra adhesive remover is "A4455".
    the extra adhesive remover is furnished to Ben.
    claim 4 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 4 is 20.
    claim 5 is for the high output pouches.
    the HCPCS code of the high output pouches is "A4413".
    the high output pouches is furnished to Ben.
    claim 5 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 5 is 45.
    the ostomy of Ben is ileostomy.
    the finding excess ostomy supplies explained about Ben is unsupported, according to the reviewer, because "the record gives no reason for more than the listed amounts".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 5 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A greater quantity than the usual maximum (90 pouches with filter in a
% month): covered on the treating practitioner's explanation in Cy's record;
% not covered where the Council finds Dee's record explains nothing — the
% Council-style unsupported finding.
scenario excess_quantity_explained is:
    claim 1 is for the pouches.
    the HCPCS code of the pouches is "A4416".
    the pouches is furnished to Cy.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 90.
    the ostomy of Cy is ileostomy.
    the finding excess ostomy supplies explained about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "high output ileostomy with peristomal skin breakdown; the pouch leaks and is changed three times a day".
    claim 2 is for the second pouches.
    the HCPCS code of the second pouches is "A4416".
    the second pouches is furnished to Dee.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 90.
    the ostomy of Dee is colostomy.
    the finding excess ostomy supplies explained about Dee is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the only explanation in the file is the supplier's note that the beneficiary asked for more pouches; the physician's notes describe a well-functioning colostomy".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Supplies used one instead of the other: Eve is furnished both the liquid
% barrier (A4369) and the barrier wipes (A5120) — neither is covered; Fay
% a night drainage bag (A4357) alone — covered; Gus both the bag and the
% bottle (A5102) — neither.
scenario one_instead_of_the_other is:
    claim 1 is for the liquid barrier.
    the HCPCS code of the liquid barrier is "A4369".
    the liquid barrier is furnished to Eve.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 2.
    claim 2 is for the barrier wipes.
    the HCPCS code of the barrier wipes is "A5120".
    the barrier wipes is furnished to Eve.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 100.
    claim 3 is for the drainage bag.
    the HCPCS code of the drainage bag is "A4357".
    the drainage bag is furnished to Fay.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 3 is 2.
    claim 4 is for the second drainage bag.
    the HCPCS code of the second drainage bag is "A4357".
    the second drainage bag is furnished to Gus.
    claim 4 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 4 is 2.
    claim 5 is for the drainage bottle.
    the HCPCS code of the drainage bottle is "A5102".
    the drainage bottle is furnished to Gus.
    claim 5 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 5 is 1.
    the ostomy of Eve is colostomy.
    the ostomy of Fay is urinary ostomy.
    the ostomy of Gus is urinary ostomy.
    rn expects answers ["claim 3 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Reasonable and necessary with its order and delivery, but Ann is in a
% covered home health episode (Policy Article A52487): the agency provides
% the supplies. Payable fails at the remedy; the flip removes the episode.
scenario home_health_episode is:
    claim 1 is for the pouches.
    the HCPCS code of the pouches is "A4416".
    the pouches is furnished to Ann.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 60.
    the ostomy of Ann is colostomy.
    the finding permanent impairment requiring ostomy about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "end colostomy after abdominoperineal resection for rectal cancer; no reversal is planned".
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "Z93.3".
    Ann is in a covered home health episode.
    the order for the pouches is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the pouches is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the pouches includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the pouches includes order date.
    the order for the pouches includes description of the item.
    the order for the pouches includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the pouches includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the pouches was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the pouches was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the pouches.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["remove: Ann is in a covered home health episode"]].

% A temporary loop ileostomy: the treating practitioner states it is
% permanent, the Council finds the record shows a reversal scheduled — the
% statutory permanence fails, and with it the claim, at the remedy.
scenario temporary_ileostomy is:
    claim 1 is for the pouches.
    the HCPCS code of the pouches is "A4416".
    the pouches is furnished to Hal.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 60.
    the ostomy of Hal is ileostomy.
    the finding permanent impairment requiring ostomy about Hal is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the operative report describes a diverting loop ileostomy and the surgeon's note schedules its reversal eight weeks later".
    the diagnosis code of Hal is "Z93.2".
    the order for the pouches is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the pouches is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the pouches includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the pouches includes order date.
    the order for the pouches includes description of the item.
    the order for the pouches includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the pouches includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the pouches was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the pouches was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the pouches.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].

% A refill of pouches, the supply running out on 1 June, the beneficiary
% contacted on 15 May and the pouches delivered on 25 May: within the
% refill windows of dmepos.le. No record of continued need is needed: the
% permanent colostomy establishes it (Policy Article A52487). A second
% refill, three months of pouches for Ann's stay in a nursing facility,
% exceeds the one-month dispensing cap.
scenario refill is:
    claim 1 is for the pouches.
    the HCPCS code of the pouches is "A4416".
    the pouches is furnished to Ann.
    claim 1 is a refill.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-25.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 60.
    the current supply of the pouches is expected to end on 2026-06-01.
    the beneficiary affirmed the need for the refill of the pouches on 2026-05-15.
    the ostomy of Ann is colostomy.
    the finding permanent impairment requiring ostomy about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "end colostomy after abdominoperineal resection for rectal cancer; no reversal is planned".
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "Z93.3".
    the order for the pouches is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the pouches is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the pouches includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the pouches includes order date.
    the order for the pouches includes description of the item.
    the order for the pouches includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the pouches includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the pouches was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the pouches was delivered on 2026-05-25.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the pouches.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The dispensing cap and the clamps: for Ida, in a nursing facility, a
% one-month supply of urostomy pouches (A4431) is payable and a three-month
% supply is not; a replacement ostomy clamp (A4363) is payable, a clamp not
% ordered as a replacement is not.
scenario nursing_facility_and_clamps is:
    claim 1 is for the urostomy pouches.
    the HCPCS code of the urostomy pouches is "A4431".
    the urostomy pouches is furnished to Ida.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 1 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 1 is 20.
    claim 2 is for the quarterly urostomy pouches.
    the HCPCS code of the quarterly urostomy pouches is "A4431".
    the quarterly urostomy pouches is furnished to Ida.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 2 is for a supply of 3 months.
    the quantity billed on claim 2 is 60.
    claim 3 is for the clamp.
    the HCPCS code of the clamp is "A4363".
    the clamp is furnished to Ida.
    the clamp was ordered as a replacement.
    the date of service of claim 3 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 3 is for a supply of 1 months.
    claim 4 is for the second clamp.
    the HCPCS code of the second clamp is "A4363".
    the second clamp is furnished to Ida.
    the date of service of claim 4 is 2026-03-01.
    claim 4 is for a supply of 1 months.
    the residence of Ida is nursing facility.
    the ostomy of Ida is urinary ostomy.
    the finding permanent impairment requiring ostomy about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "ileal conduit after cystectomy".
    the diagnosis code of Ida is "Z93.6".
    the order for the urostomy pouches is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the urostomy pouches is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the urostomy pouches includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the urostomy pouches includes order date.
    the order for the urostomy pouches includes description of the item.
    the order for the urostomy pouches includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the urostomy pouches includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the urostomy pouches was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the urostomy pouches was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the urostomy pouches.
    the order for the quarterly urostomy pouches is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the quarterly urostomy pouches is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the quarterly urostomy pouches includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the quarterly urostomy pouches includes order date.
    the order for the quarterly urostomy pouches includes description of the item.
    the order for the quarterly urostomy pouches includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the quarterly urostomy pouches includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the quarterly urostomy pouches was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the quarterly urostomy pouches was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the quarterly urostomy pouches.
    the order for the clamp is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the clamp is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the clamp includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the clamp includes order date.
    the order for the clamp includes description of the item.
    the order for the clamp includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the clamp includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the clamp was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the clamp was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the clamp.
    the order for the second clamp is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the second clamp is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the second clamp includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the second clamp includes order date.
    the order for the second clamp includes description of the item.
    the order for the second clamp includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the second clamp includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the second clamp was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the second clamp was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the second clamp.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable", "claim 3 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 4 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].
